# Let It Be, refrain (figure 165.2)
# Three upper voices over the chords in the first phrase, as Pollack types them; the E held through
# bars 1-3 makes bar 2 (G in the bass) sound as much like V with added sixth as iii 6/5. Alto and
# tenor move in parallel thirds. The second phrase is chords only.
#? Octaves: a close voicing around middle C (soprano E4, alto E4-C4, tenor C4-G3), with soprano and alto in unison in bars 1 and 4 as typed; the voices may be spaced more widely on the record.
